replies.text:
@HiddenCanada Sure, we lived on Westlake rd. not far from the lodge, 1 minute drive. We see a couple firetrucks go past, of course we all jumped in our cars to follow, I was 16 at the time. A few neighbours had followed so there was a small crowd, I remember it was dark, and it didn't take long to figure out where they were going, it is a very bendy road at end of our street that only led to the lodge and dunes. 
By the time we got there, the whole place was lit up. The fire kept jumping to the trees, but the fire department handled it. I don’t remember much else, it was pretty incredible to see it.
I honestly haven’t thought about that night in years. I was just enjoying seeing all the familiar places, and then you mentioned the fire and I was like, wow, someone’s talking about that fire after all this time. Your videos are amazing.
